{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["In my view the first journey alone was unlike the other journeys, and the verse that says 'the Kohathites set out after the two standards' applies to all the journeys except this one, for the Ark traveled ahead of them. This was for three days only, and this is the meaning of 'a journey of three days.' Its parallel is 'they went three days in the wilderness.' 'Etam' — its meaning is not that they traveled in one day the distance of three days. Some say they traveled the distance of three days in one day. Some say they traveled the distance of three days corresponding to the journeys they made when they went out of Egypt, and the Ark was distant from them a distance of three days. This is the meaning [they propose], and 'the cloud settled in the wilderness of Paran' — they explain 'they set out on the first journey' [as meaning] that by the mouth of Moses they set out, for the cloud moved immediately. This is impossible, for Moses would not depart from the Ark, and the proof is 'when the Ark set out, Moses said,' and when it rested, he said. The correct view in my eyes is what I have said. And the meaning of 'the cloud settled in the wilderness of Paran' is a general statement encompassing Taberah, which is Kivrot HaTa'avah, and Hatzerot, and Ritmah, and many journeys. The proof is that Scripture does not mention 'the wilderness of Paran' in the section of 'These are the journeys,' and I shall explain further:" "And the meaning of <b>by the mouth of YHWH</b> is: at the sounding of the trumpets."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The text reads איתם, likely referring to the place name Etham/Itam mentioned in the wilderness itinerary; translated as a place name with minimal gloss."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:08.790446572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}